Below is the **updated implementation** that respects a typing speed of **300 words / minute** (≈ 25 characters / second) while keeping the *delay‑before‑start* at its default (0 s).  

The only change from the previous version is that the animation **duration is calculated on‑the‑fly** from the number of characters the user has typed, so the effect always runs at the requested speed.

---

## 1. Quick‑look at the math  

* 300 wpm → 5 words / s.  
* Average English word ≈ 5 characters → **25 characters / s**.  
* One character therefore takes **0.04 s** (40 ms).  

So for a string that contains *N* characters the animation should run for **N × 0.04 s**.

---

## 2. Full working example (copy‑paste)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Form – typing animation @ 300 wpm</title>
<style>
/* -------------------------------------------------
   Layout
------------------------------------------------- */
.typing-form {
  max-width: 420px;
  margin: 2rem auto;
  font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
}
.typing-field {
  position: relative;
  margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
}

/* -------------------------------------------------
   Real input / textarea (transparent background)
------------------------------------------------- */
.typing-field input,
.typing-field textarea {
  width: 100%;
  padding: .6rem .8rem;
  font-size: 1rem;
  line-height: 1.4;
  border: 2px solid #bbb;
  border-radius: 4px;
  background: transparent;
  color: #333;
  position: relative;
  z-index: 2;               /* keep it above the mirror */
}

/* -------------------------------------------------
   Mirror element – hidden but used for animation
------------------------------------------------- */
.typing-field .mirror {
  position: absolute;
  top: .6rem; left: .8rem;
  font-size: 1rem;
  line-height: 1.4;
  white-space: pre;        /* preserve spaces */
  overflow: hidden;
  pointer-events: none;
  color: transparent;      /* we only need its width */
  z-index: 1;
}

/* -------------------------------------------------
   Blinking caret (cursor)
------------------------------------------------- */
.typing-field::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  top: .6rem; left: .8rem;
  width: 2px;
  height: 1.2rem;
  background: #333;
  animation: blink .8s steps(1) infinite;
  z-index: 3;
}

/* -------------------------------------------------
   Typewriter animation (width grows from 0 → full)
------------------------------------------------- */
@keyframes typewriter {
  from { width: 0; }
  to   { width: var(--text-width); }
}
@keyframes blink {
  0%, 50% { opacity: 1; }
  51%, 100% { opacity: 0; }
}

/* -------------------------------------------------
   When the user is typing we add the .typing class.
   The animation duration is set via the CSS variable
   --type-duration (calculated in JS).
------------------------------------------------- */
.typing-field.typing .mirror {
  animation:
    typewriter var(--type-duration) steps(var(--char-count)) forwards;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<form class="typing-form">
  <div class="typing-field">
    <input type="text" id="name" name="name" placeholder="Your name">
    <span class="mirror" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </div>

  <div class="typing-field">
    <textarea id="msg" name="msg" rows="4" placeholder="Your message"></textarea>
    <span class="mirror" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </div>

  <button type="submit">Send</button>
</form>

<script>
/* -------------------------------------------------
   Helper – copy typographic styles from the real
   field to the hidden mirror so width measurement is
   pixel‑perfect.
------------------------------------------------- */
function syncStyles(input, mirror) {
  const style = window.getComputedStyle(input);
  const props = [
    'fontFamily','fontSize','fontWeight','fontStyle',
    'letterSpacing','textTransform','textIndent',
    'padding','border','boxSizing','lineHeight'
  ];
  props.forEach(p => mirror.style[p] = style[p]);
}

/* -------------------------------------------------
   Main – attach listeners to every .typing-field
------------------------------------------------- */
document.querySelectorAll('.typing-field').forEach(wrapper => {
  const input  = wrapper.querySelector('input, textarea');
  const mirror = wrapper.querySelector('.mirror');

  // Initial sync (placeholder text must NOT be animated)
  syncStyles(input, mirror);
  mirror.textContent = '';

  const animate = () => {
    const value = input.value;
    mirror.textContent = value;               // mirror gets the raw text

    // ---- 1️⃣ Measure the exact width of the text -----------------
    const width = mirror.getBoundingClientRect().width + 2; // +2 px safety
    wrapper.style.setProperty('--text-width', `${width}px`);

    // ---- 2️⃣ Number of characters (used for steps()) ------------
    const charCount = value.length;
    wrapper.style.setProperty('--char-count', charCount);

    // ---- 3️⃣ Duration based on 300 wpm (≈ 25 chars / s) ---------
    // 1 character → 0.04 s  (40 ms)
    const duration = (charCount * 0.04).toFixed(3); // seconds, 3 dp
    wrapper.style.setProperty('--type-duration', `${duration}s`);

    // ---- 4️⃣ Restart the animation -------------------------------
    wrapper.classList.remove('typing');
    // Force re‑flow so the removal is noticed
    void wrapper.offsetWidth;
    wrapper.classList.add('typing');
  };

  // Run on every keystroke and also when the field receives focus
  input.addEventListener('input', animate);
  input.addEventListener('focus', animate);
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What changed?

| Part | Change |
|------|--------|
| **CSS** | The `.mirror` animation now uses `var(--type-duration)` for its duration. |
| **JS** | After each keystroke we compute `duration = characters × 0.04 s` (the 300 wpm speed) and store it in `--type-duration`. The delay‑before‑start stays at the default (`0 s`). |
| **HTML** | No change – the same markup works. |

---

## 3. How to adapt the speed (if you ever need a different WPM)

```js
// Desired words‑per‑minute (WPM)
const WPM = 300;                     // ← change this number
const charsPerSec = (WPM * 5) / 60;  // 5 chars ≈ 1 word
const secPerChar = 1 / charsPerSec; // seconds per character

// Inside the animate() function:
const duration = (charCount * secPerChar).toFixed(3);
wrapper.style.setProperty('--type-duration', `${duration}s`);
```

Just replace the constant `WPM` with any other value and the animation will automatically adjust.

